<DocLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement | Dazzlit"
  description="Dazzlit's commitment to making dazzlit.com accessible to everyone."
  canonicalPath="/accessibility/"
  heading="Accessibility Statement"
  updated="16 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    Dazzlit wants everyone to be able to use dazzlit.com, including people
    who use screen readers, keyboard navigation or other assistive
    technologies. We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
    (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA across the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pages are built with semantic headings, labels and landmarks so assistive technologies can follow the structure.</li>
    <li>Text and interactive elements are designed to meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast requirements, and the site can be used by keyboard alone.</li>
    <li>Images carry alternative text, and the site is tested for keyboard navigation and screen reader use as part of our build checks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <p>Some older content and third-party embeds may not yet fully meet these standards. We are working through them as pages are built and reviewed.</p>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>If you find a barrier on this site, or need information in another format, please tell us through the form on our contact page, describing the page and the problem. We will do our best to fix it or provide the information another way.</p>
</DocLayout>
